-- title:
--   The finite-sample Gaussian Taylor residual
-- statement:
--   For sample size \(n\), observation-radius parameter \(T\), location-radius parameter \(S\), and Taylor order \(L\), define
--   \[
--   \mathcal R(n,T,S,L)
--   =\sqrt n\,e^{\,2TS+S^2/2}\frac{(TS)^{L+1}}{(L+1)!}.
--   \]
--   For nonnegative radii this is the explicit residual scale in the Gaussian dictionary's Taylor approximation. The factorial term records truncation after degree \(L\), the exponential term controls the remainder uniformly over the two radius constraints, and the factor \(\sqrt n\) converts coordinatewise control to the Euclidean norm of the \(n\)-dimensional fitted vector.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/hanshengjiang/reweighted-npmle-lean/blob/5af8d16822c5a8a3f032b13eb95daea40f307484/ReweightedNPMLE/GaussianStructural.lean#L103-L105

